2026-09-27T07:42:49.7646052Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7646419Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7646773Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7647403Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7648016Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7648085Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7648239Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7648458Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7648653Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7648721Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7648882Z ================
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7648977Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7649092Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7649357Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7649506Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7649599Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7649808Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7649968Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7650074Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7650343Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7650597Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7651077Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7651462Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7651549Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7652061Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7652518Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7652715Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7652933Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7710736Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7710855Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7711076Z ========
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7711202Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7712715Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7714319Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7714582Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7715056Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7715961Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7716557Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7717208Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7717723Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7718186Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7718307Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7718592Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7718764Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7720006Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7721436Z 
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7722390Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7723492Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:42:49.7723733Z 
